# Notices

## Intel Graphics Control Library (IGCL)

`src-tauri/src/backend/intel.rs` contains C struct definitions and constant
names transcribed from the public Intel SDK header `igcl_api.h` of the
Intel Graphics Control Library:

- Source: https://github.com/intel/drivers.gpu.control-library
- Header: `include/igcl_api.h`
- Copyright (C) 2025 Intel Corporation
- License: Intel Software License Agreement 10.07.21
  (license text: https://github.com/intel/drivers.gpu.control-library/blob/master/LICENSE)

The header is redistributed by Intel with notice, "solely for use on Intel
platforms". Only the minimal subset of types actually used by ChromaDeck is
reproduced, with names preserved verbatim (including upstream spellings such
as `CTL_PIXTX_CONFIG_OPERTAION_TYPE_*` and the transcribed struct
`ctl_adapter_display_encoder_properties_t`), together with the matching
function-pointer typedefs. No function implementation is transcribed; driver
entry points are resolved dynamically by name at runtime.

ChromaDeck does not redistribute any Intel binaries. The Intel driver
libraries (`ControlLib.dll`, `IntelControlLib.dll`) are loaded at runtime
from the local Windows DriverStore, and only their exported symbols and the
public header are used. No Intel binary is reverse-engineered.

## nvBrightness

[nvBrightness](https://github.com/pbatard/nvBrightness) by Pete Batard was
used as a behavioral reference for NVIDIA's brightness transfer math. No code
is reused; the math is reimplemented from observed driver behavior.

## NvAPIWrapper

[NvAPIWrapper](https://github.com/falahati/NvAPIWrapper) was used as a
reference for NVAPI interface IDs. No code is reused.
